{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:14.35.010","page_type":"section"},"citation":"14.35.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.35.010","content_hash":"71e7efd0b706bcf91244c1b6caf7b46319f49169f10050135bc36ae979a85f7e","heading":"Uniform Plumbing Code – Adopted.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.35.010:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.35.010","text":"(a) The 2024 Uniform Plumbing Code, including all appendices, is hereby adopted by reference and made part of the code for the city. The 2024 Uniform Plumbing Code Illustrated Training Manual and the 2024 Uniform Plumbing Code Answers and Analysis Manual as published by the International Association of Plumbing and Mechanical Officials may be considered and applied by the authority having jurisdiction to the extent necessary in the authority’s sole discretion to implement and enforce this code.\n(b) The following appendices are hereby adopted:\nAppendix A – Recommended Rules for Sizing the Water Supply System.\nAppendix B – Explanatory Notes on Combination Waste and Vent Systems.\nAppendix C – Alternate Plumbing Systems.\nAppendix D – Sizing Stormwater Drainage Systems.\nAppendix E – Manufactured/Mobile Home Parks and Recreational Vehicle Parks.\nAppendix G – Sizing of Venting Systems.\nAppendix H – Private Sewage Disposal Systems.\nAppendix I – Installation Standard for PEX Tubing Systems for Hot- and Cold-Water Distribution and the Installation Standards for Trenchless Insertion of Polyethylene (PE) Pipe for Sewer Laterals.\nAppendix J – Combination of Indoor and Outdoor Combustion and Ventilation Opening Design.\nAppendix K – Potable Rainwater Catchment Systems.\nAppendix L – Sustainable Practices.\nAppendix M – Peak Water Demand Calculator.\nAppendix N – Impact of Water Temperature on the Potential for Scalding and Legionella Growth.\nAppendix O – Non-Sewered Sanitation Systems.\nAppendix P – Professional Qualifications.\nAppendix Q – Indoor Horticultural Facilities.\nAppendix R – Tiny Houses.\nAppendix S – On-Site Stormwater Treatment Systems. (Ord. 20570 § 1, 7-1-25.)","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"a6790f55-a095-5649-b2ab-679c70366b98"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"14.35.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.35.010","content_hash":"c1e09ca97ec9c26d4cba720fd5d4d73db52dcbafea89c0bb83f0cf04cb1d1281","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.35.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.35.010:block:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.35.010","text":"(a) The 2024 Uniform Plumbing Code, including all appendices, is hereby adopted by reference and made part of the code for the city. The 2024 Uniform Plumbing Code Illustrated Training Manual and the 2024 Uniform Plumbing Code Answers and Analysis Manual as published by the International Association of Plumbing and Mechanical Officials may be considered and applied by the authority having jurisdiction to the extent necessary in the authority’s sole discretion to implement and enforce this code.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"08fc9d1d-b9d8-5d2b-a7b2-eff22f78f9b6"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"14.35.010","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.35.010","content_hash":"40f956874b887a20720e884a0da710c40a39a6fa68d32d50f990720c9c321eeb","heading":null,"ordinal":1,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.35.010:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.35.010:block:1","source_url":"https://